---
// Beat 2 — The moment (docs/copy-deck.md Beat 2, docs/demo-script.md).
// The single most important section on the page — "the product's trailer"
// (PRD §6). Section markup here is deliberately thin: a heading, one line
// above the demo, and the demo itself. No other copy in this section.
//
// Two renderings of the same beat-script, chosen purely by CSS
// (`motion-reduce:`) so there is never a client-side reduced-motion check
// racing against first paint:
//   1. TerminalDemo (client:media, motion-reduce:hidden) — the animated
//      beat-script player. `client:media="(prefers-reduced-motion:
//      no-preference)"` means its JS is never fetched or hydrated at all for
//      a visitor who prefers reduced motion.
//   2. A fully static, zero-JS fallback (hidden by default, `motion-reduce:
//      block`) built from the same TerminalFrame chrome used elsewhere on
//      the site: Act 1's final frame and Act 2's final frame, stacked, with
//      the scene-break stamp between them — exactly per demo-script.md's
//      reduced-motion direction. Zero animation.
//
// A single sr-only transcript (verbatim strings from demo-script.md) covers
// both renderings for assistive tech, so the constantly-updating animated
// text never has to be exposed to (and re-announced by) a screen reader —
// both visual containers are aria-hidden; the pause/play control is not.
import TerminalDemo from "../components/TerminalDemo";
import TerminalFrame from "../components/TerminalFrame.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
---

<section id="demo" data-beat="2-demo">
  <div class="container-field flex flex-col gap-10">
    <div class="typeset mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-medium text-forest-600">
        The moment it pays off.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-ink leading-relaxed">
        You never search. You never remember. It just shows up.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl">
      <!-- Animated beat-script player (no JS shipped for reduced-motion visitors). -->
      <div class="motion-reduce:hidden">
        <TerminalDemo client:media="(prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)" />
      </div>

      <!-- Static, zero-JS fallback: two final frames + scene-break stamp. -->
      <div class="hidden flex-col gap-6 motion-reduce:flex" aria-hidden="true">
        <TerminalFrame title="side-project · claude">
          <div class="space-y-1.5">
            <p class="text-ink font-medium">
              <span class="mr-2 select-none text-forest-600">❯</span>/scout:add
              https://github.com/clauderic/dnd-kit
            </p>
            <div
              class="my-1 space-y-1 rounded-md border border-ink/15 bg-paper-100/70 px-3 py-2.5"
            >
              <p class="text-ink-muted">
                dnd-kit — modular drag-and-drop toolkit for React
              </p>
              <p class="text-ink-muted">
                packs when: drag-and-drop, sortable lists, draggable UI
              </p>
              <p class="text-ink-muted">Add to pack? (y/n) y</p>
            </div>
            <p class="font-medium text-forest-600">✓ Packed.</p>
          </div>
        </TerminalFrame>

        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-2 py-2 text-center">
          <Icon name="waypoint" size={18} class="shrink-0 text-trail-500" />
          <span
            class="italic text-ink-muted"
            style="font-family: var(--font-heading);"
          >
            — days later, a different project —
          </span>
        </div>

        <TerminalFrame title="kanban-board · claude">
          <div class="space-y-1.5">
            <p class="text-ink font-medium">
              <span class="mr-2 select-none text-forest-600">❯</span>make the
              board cards draggable between columns
            </p>
            <p class="text-ink-faint italic">
              Planning: board view, drag layer, column drop targets…
            </p>
            <div class="my-1 space-y-1 rounded-md border border-ink/15 bg-paper-100/70 px-3 py-2.5">
              <p class="font-medium" style="color: var(--color-report);">
                ⌖ dnd-kit — github.com/clauderic/dnd-kit
              </p>
              <p class="pl-[2ch] text-ink">
                Modular drag-and-drop toolkit for React.
              </p>
              <p class="pl-[2ch] text-ink">
                Matched: "drag-and-drop, sortable lists, draggable UI"
              </p>
            </div>
            <p class="text-ink">Using dnd-kit for the drag layer.</p>
            <p class="font-medium text-forest-600">
              ✓ Cards draggable between columns.
            </p>
          </div>
        </TerminalFrame>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="sr-only">
      Demo transcript. First, an existing project: the developer runs
      /scout:add https://github.com/clauderic/dnd-kit. Scout drafts an entry —
      dnd-kit, a modular drag-and-drop toolkit for React, that packs when
      drag-and-drop, sortable lists, or draggable UI are involved — and asks
      "Add to pack?". The developer answers y, and it's packed. Days later, a
      different project: the developer asks their agent to make the board
      cards draggable between columns. Mid-plan, a report appears on its own:
      "dnd-kit — github.com/clauderic/dnd-kit. Modular drag-and-drop toolkit
      for React. Matched: drag-and-drop, sortable lists, draggable UI." The
      agent uses dnd-kit for the drag layer, and the cards become draggable
      between columns.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
